+# Later severity steering
+
+After the first candidate's source-use calls ended, the owner added:
+
+> the review means the bugs can be assigned a severity of 1-5
+
+> generally 3 is the one that can go either way, if it has downstream impact and broader splash zone probably needs to be fixed
+
+The Executive binds the selected convention as 1 highest–5 lowest. Reviewer
+grades consequence; Executive retains that grade and separately decides
+priority/disposition. Product-specific evidence criteria remain explicit.
+Severity 3 requires downstream/blast-radius assessment, with repair normally
+selected for material dependent impact and reason/owner retained for a lawful
+contained-local deferral. No automatic priority, hard-stop or boundary mapping
+is authorized, and older/alternative scales are not relabelled.
+
+The original [source delta](SOURCE_DELTA.json), SHA-256
+`5d99a826ccedb5257aa5c01b92e5347f4fed43271123526c73a4e501d1bf7810`,
+is unchanged. Its 25 changed source files and full package inventory are retained
+under [candidate-001](candidate-001/RETENTION.json); unchanged source remains
+the Git predecessor `8a756806c7ec5063ad7afbaff50d837882a33f12`.
+The original native observations retain that subject and their scenario scale.
+
+The Executive separately records the E1 source-use limitation: the actor's
+[actual return](testing/runs/E1/FINAL.txt) labelled a combined next review
+already authorized while its grouping was unresolved and presumed a repair
+Writer grant absent from the scenario. No dispatch occurred. This is operational
+evidence, not a finding of contradictory normative text. A concise readiness
+reminder may clarify the existing intake law; parser/gate semantics do not
+change. Raw-JSON transport failures remain fixture/actor limitations.
+
+The bounded successor receives source and mechanical checks only. No further
+native calls, installation, consumer adoption, Git mutation or release is
+selected in this activation.
